[center][color=#00f0ff][size=6][b]NC ZONING BOARD[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#8892b0]NIGHT CORP // URBAN PLANNING DIVISION[/color]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]INSTRUMENT NC-ZB-02 - THE DISTRICT GUIDE[/b][/size][/color]
[i]Which location mods are in the district around you - in game, on the map, and on a shelf you can browse.[/i][/center]
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]0. NATURE OF THIS INSTRUMENT[/b][/size][/color]
The [b]NC Zoning Board - District Guide[/b] brings the [url=https://nczoning.net]NC Zoning Board[/url] map into the game. It knows which district you are standing in, and it tells you what the Board has on file for it.

Four surfaces, all built out of the game's own UI - no ImGui window, no separate overlay:
[list]
[*][b]A district notice.[/b] Cross into a new district and a panel appears under the game's own district banner: how many mapped locations are here, and the nearest one by name.
[*][b]The world map.[/b] Hover any district and its info panel gains a count and a category breakdown, in the map's own type and colors.
[*][b]The guide.[/b] One key opens a full browser: every district, every location, with images, search, and a jump straight to any of them.
[*][b]Fast travel.[/b] Arriving somewhere fires no district banner in vanilla, so the notice shows up on its own.
[/list]
[color=#ffb300][b]It never suppresses or alters anything the game already draws.[/b][/color] Every hook adds; none replaces. With every feature switched off, the game behaves exactly as if the mod were not installed.
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]1. THE WIDER PROJECT[/b][/size][/color]
The Guide is the in-game window onto [b]NC Zoning Board[/b], the interactive map of Cyberpunk 2077 location mods.
[list]
[*][b]Explore the map:[/b] [url=https://nczoning.net]nczoning.net[/url]
[*][b]Join the community:[/b] [url=https://discord.gg/sc4yEx2fNf]Locations Hub Discord[/url]
[/list]
[center][b]Showcase[/b]
[youtube]30Daism2E-c[/youtube]
[b]Trailer[/b]
[youtube]LJVJ2lN4aQ0[/youtube][/center]
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]2. THE GUIDE[/b][/size][/color]
A gallery of location mods, filed by district.
[list]
[*][b]Browse by district and subdistrict[/b] - the list opens on wherever you are standing by default.
[*][b]Search[/b] by name, author or tags from the Map site.
[*][b]Photographs.[/b] Each card carries the location's survey image where the registry has one.
[*][b]Show on map.[/b] One click drops a waypoint on the location, opens the world map on it and starts tracking. No hunting for the pin, no tracking it by hand.
[*][b]Teleport[/b] straight to it, if you would rather skip the drive.
[*][b]Recently updated[/b] locations are flagged in green on the card image and sorted to the top, so a district you know still shows you what changed.
[*][b]Already installed?[/b] Cards for mods you have carry a cyan INSTALLED badge.
[/list]

[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]2a. THE INSTALL FILTER[/b][/size][/color]
With [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url][/b] installed, the guide marks which of these location mods you already have. One button cycles the whole list:
[list]
[*][b]ALL[/b] - every location on file.
[*][b]INSTALLED[/b] - only the ones already on your machine.
[*][b]MISSING[/b] - only the ones you do not have.
[*][b]UNKNOWN[/b] - the ones that cannot be detected either way. AMM location mods are the usual case: they ship a single file into CET's own folder, which no mod can read.
[/list]
[i]Without CET the filter button is hidden. Everything else works exactly as described.[/i]
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]3. A KNOWN LIMIT OF THE ROAD NETWORK[/b][/size][/color]
A waypoint only starts routing once the world map has been opened. That is the game's own behavior: only the map can adopt a script-placed pin as your tracked waypoint.

The guide opens the map and tracks the waypoint for you by default. If you switch both [b]Open the Map on Show[/b] and [b]Track the Waypoint[/b] off: the pin is placed, and it draws no route until you open the map and track it yourself.
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]4. SETTINGS[/b][/size][/color]
Everything is in the [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/b] overlay - press [b]F8[/b] in game.
[list]
[*][b]Narrow to Subdistrict.[/b] Scopes every count to your subdistrict when you are in one, rather than the whole district. Applies to all four surfaces.
[*][b]Enable District Guide.[/b] Turns the browser on or off.
[*][b]Open Guide Key.[/b] The key that opens it. Needs Input Loader.
[*][b]Open Guide Modifier.[/b] An optional key to hold alongside it. Any key, not just Shift, Alt or Ctrl. Leave unset for none.
[*][b]Open Guide Showing.[/b] Which locations the guide lists when it opens. Needs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] installed - the Core detects your installed mods through it.
[*][b]Open on Your District.[/b] The guide opens on the district you are standing in. Off opens it on ALL LOCATIONS.
[*][b]Open the Map on Show.[/b] SHOW ON MAP opens the world map and centers it on the waypoint. Off places the waypoint and leaves you in the guide.
[*][b]Track the Waypoint.[/b] Routes to the waypoint straight away. This replaces a custom waypoint you have placed; your tracked quest is a separate slot and is left alone.
[*][b]Show on World Map.[/b] Adds the count and category breakdown to the map's district info panel.
[*][b]Enable District Notice.[/b] The panel under the game's district banner.
[*][b]Name the Nearest Location.[/b] Also names the closest location in the area. Off shows only the count.
[*][b]Show on Fast Travel.[/b] The arrival panel after a fast travel. Off leaves fast travel entirely to the game.
[/list]
The mod runs on its defaults without RCF; you simply cannot rebind anything.

[i]The full documentation is also readable in game, in the RCF hub under DOCS.[/i]
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]5. CONDITIONS OF ISSUE[/b][/size][/color]
[b]Required:[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/31920]RedLogger[/url]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/32277]NC Zoning Board - Core[/url][/b], and its own requirements
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] - for the rebindable key
[/list]
[color=#ffb300][b]NC Zoning Board - Core 1.0.0 or newer is a hard requirement.[/b][/color] Redscript compiles every installed mod as one unit, so an older Core is a compile failure that takes down [i]every[/i] redscript mod on your machine, not just this one. The two release together.

[b]Strongly recommended:[/b]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/b] - the only settings UI. Without it nothing can be rebound.
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url][/b] - what detects which location mods you already have.
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/31941]RedIMGRetriever[/url][/b] - what fetches the card images. Without it the cards show a placeholder and everything else is unchanged.
[/list]
[i]The mod is whole without the three optional ones. Each removes a feature, not the mod.[/i]
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]6. INSTALLATION[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*]Install the requirements above, the Core included.
[*]Download this mod and extract the [font=Courier New]r6[/font] folder into your Cyberpunk 2077 root directory.
[i]Final path should look like:[/i] [font=Courier New]Cyberpunk 2077\r6\scripts\NCZoningDistrictGuide\[/font]
[*]Load a save. Press [b]'[/b] (apostrophe) to open the guide, or rebind it in the F8 panel.
[/list]
Works with mod managers, or install manually.
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]7. WHERE THE DATA COMES FROM[/b][/size][/color]
Everything shown here is the [b]NC Zoning Board[/b] registry, maintained by the community at [url=https://nczoning.net]nczoning.net[/url]. This mod displays it; the [b]Core[/b] fetches it. If a location mod is missing from the guide, it is missing from the registry - and the map is open for submissions.
[line]
[color=#00f0ff][size=5][b]8. COMPATIBILITY[/b][/size][/color]
Every hook this mod places calls the original code first and unconditionally, then adds a widget beside it. Nothing the game already draws is replaced or suppressed, so other mods touching the same controllers keep working.

It is pure redscript with no [font=Courier New].archive[/font] file, so it cannot conflict with anything over game assets.
[line]
